{
  "source": "video-audit/build-skills-opener-v14-2026-11-11/edited.wav",
  "duration": 107.1666875,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.16,
      "text": "The AI platforms we rely on are caught in an endless cycle of updates, overhauls, and inevitable"
    },
    {
      "start": 6.16,
      "end": 11.24,
      "text": "obsolescence. Think back to the very first time you learned how to ride a bicycle. The actual"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.24,
      "end": 16.84,
      "text": "achievement happening in your brain was developing a physical sense of balance. Fast forward a few"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.84,
      "end": 21.88,
      "text": "years and you outgrew that childhood bike. You banded it in the garage and eventually moved on to"
    },
    {
      "start": 21.88,
      "end": 27.02,
      "text": "something else. You took that ingrained sense of balance and applied it to entirely different"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.02,
      "end": 32.68,
      "text": "physical environments. It is the exact same core mechanism that kept you upright the first time"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.68,
      "end": 37.78,
      "text": "you tried ice skating. No one could download that coordination into your nervous system and you"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.78,
      "end": 42.54,
      "text": "couldn't buy it off a shelf. You had to earn it through the friction of your own practice."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.42,
      "end": 48.58,
      "text": "That physical dynamic maps directly onto intellectual development in the modern classroom and workplace,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.1,
      "end": 54.52,
      "text": "thinking carefully, working alongside others, hunting for fresh ideas, and maintaining an"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.52,
      "end": 59.92,
      "text": "active curiosity. You will use AI to practice, but the mental agility you build in the process"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.92,
      "end": 65.44,
      "text": "goes with you everywhere. It shapes how you approach an essay in school, how you solve a bottleneck at"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.44,
      "end": 71.06,
      "text": "work, and how you organize your daily life. When the technical tools are identical across the board,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.52,
      "end": 77.2,
      "text": "the only variables left are your unique choices, the specific questions you ask, and the cultivated"
    },
    {
      "start": 77.2,
      "end": 82.5,
      "text": "judgment you apply to the output. This section will help you answer three specific questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.3,
      "end": 89.66,
      "text": "What will set me apart in a world with AI? Next question two, what skills should I start building"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.66,
      "end": 96.12,
      "text": "now? Finally question three, how can I use AI effectively and responsibly in my future work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.8,
      "end": 100.04,
      "text": "The tools will change. The skills are yours to keep."
    }
  ],
